2060 0 obj
  << /ActualText (1\056 LEVEL CONCEPT\n\nA military officer is trapped inside a prison overtaken by a mafia gang attempting to free their boss\056 All exits are blocked\056 The only way out is the helicopter extraction point on Tower 1\056 The player must navigate through four towers\054 a hostile courtyard\054 and escalating enemy presence \024 managing limited resources and making real\055time decisions under pressure\056\nThe level is designed around one core promise\072 every major decision belongs to the player\056 Stealth and combat are equally valid at every encounter\056 Exploration is rewarded but never required\056 The environment guides without instructing\056)
     /K [ 20 ]
     /P 2061 0 R
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2061 0 obj
  << /K [ 2060 0 R ]
     /P 2198 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2062 0 obj
  << /ActualText (2\056 DESIGN PILLARS\n\nPillar 1 \024 Player Agency Every major encounter and traversal section supports both stealth and combat\056 The player is never forced into a single approach\056 Both paths are challenging\054 both are valid\054 both lead to the same destination\056\n\nPillar 2 \024 Environment as Teacher No waypoints\056 No mini maps\056 The environment communicates through lighting\054 spatial design\054 and prop placement\056 The player learns through observation and action\054 not instruction\056\n\nPillar 3 \024 Deliberate Escalation Intensity builds across all six beats \024 introducing mechanics one at a time\054 layering complexity only after the player has demonstrated understanding\056 The player is never overwhelmed before they are ready\056\n\nPillar 4 \024 Exploration Has Value Optional routes reward players with better weapons and tactical information\056 Players who push straight through still progress\056 Curiosity is rewarded\054 never required\056\n\nPillar 5 \024 Narrative Through Space No cutscenes\056 No forced dialogue\056 The story is told through readable notes\054 proximity\055triggered monologues\054 environmental lighting\054 and spatial context\056 The player uncovers the situation at their own pace\056)
     /K [ 21 ]
     /P 2063 0 R
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2063 0 obj
  << /K [ 2062 0 R ]
     /P 2198 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2064 0 obj
  << /ActualText (3\056 PLAYER FANTASY\n\nThe player should feel like a tactical military officer \024 calm under pressure\054 resourceful\054 and always one decision ahead of the chaos around them\056 Not a superhero\056 Not helpless\056 Someone who reads a room\054 makes a call\054 and lives with the consequences\056)
     /K [ 22 ]
     /P 2065 0 R
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2065 0 obj
  << /K [ 2064 0 R ]
     /P 2198 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2066 0 obj
  << /ActualText (4\056 LEVEL LAYOUT\n\nMacro Structure\nEscape Protocol is organised around four towers \024 T1\054 T2\054 T3\054 T4 \024 connected by bridges\054 with an open central courtyard between them\056 The prison sits in a remote canyon\054 completely isolated\056)
     /K [ 23 ]
     /P 2067 0 R
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

