endobj

2190 0 obj
  << /ActualText (11\056 ENVIRONMENTAL STORYTELLING\n\nNo cutscenes\056 No forced stops\056 The story is told entirely through readable notes\054 fax documents\054 proximity monologues\054 and the environment itself \024 collapsed structures\054 debris\054 and siege damage communicate the prison\047s state without a single line of exposition\056 Players who engage with the environment get the full story\056 Players who push forward still understand their objective\056 The fax document in Beat 5 is the narrative turning point \024 up to that moment the player was surviving on instinct\054 after reading it they have a clear destination and a sense of urgency\056)
     /K [ 85 ]
     /P 2191 0 R
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2191 0 obj
  << /K [ 2190 0 R ]
     /P 2198 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2192 0 obj
  << /ActualText (12\056 LIGHTING DESIGN\n\nRed emergency lighting serves as both atmosphere and navigation throughout all interior spaces\056 Outdoors\054 natural canyon daylight creates immediate contrast \024 the player always knows whether they are inside or outside\056 Subtle red cues mark optional reward locations for attentive players without making them obvious\056 Beat 3 removes red light entirely\054 using darkness as a deliberate tension mechanic rather than a technical limitation\056)
     /K [ 86 ]
     /P 2193 0 R
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2193 0 obj
  << /K [ 2192 0 R ]
     /P 2198 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2194 0 obj
  << /ActualText (13\056 TRAVERSAL DESIGN\n\nEvery traversal mechanic is introduced in Beat 1 through environmental design \024 each one required to progress\054 each encountered before it becomes critical later\056 Ledge climbing complexity increases deliberately across the level\056 Beats 1 through 4 use linear sequences \024 up\054 down\054 left\054 right\056 Beat 5 places ledges directly opposite each other\054 requiring simultaneous camera movement and grab input\056 Players who had built instinct through earlier beats navigated this naturally without a single prompt\056)
     /K [ 87 ]
     /P 2195 0 R
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2195 0 obj
  << /K [ 2194 0 R ]
     /P 2198 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

2196 0 obj
  << /ActualText (14\056 TECHNICAL NOTES\n\nBuilt in Unreal Engine 5\0567 using AGLS by LongmireLocomotion for all locomotion and animation systems\056 All interactive logic\054 triggered sequences\054 and monologue systems were built using Blueprint Visual Scripting\056\nAGLS does not include a native health pickup system\056 Rather than engineering a workaround\054 encounters were restructured so skilled players would rarely lose health \024 reducing enemy numbers\054 simplifying combat sequences\054 and shifting design focus toward traversal and spatial clarity\056 This constraint produced a cleaner\054 more intentional encounter structure than the original design intended\056)
     /K [ 88 ]
     /P 2197 0 R
     /Pg 2020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

